# A bug of the prototype (Nov 2004 debug build; the code matches the GameCube SHA1). Ashley waiting
# (F_STAY) calls "Help!" every 151 frames while a living enemy is within 4 m and Leon is more than
# 2 m away (cSubChar::moveFootwork, pl_npc.cpp; the enemy count skips ids above 0x3F, hp 0 and
# EM_STATUS_ASHLEY_NO_HELP). The shooting range r22c parks Ashley at (-1600, 0, -270) next to its
# two gates, built as targets (cEmMark, em 0x3E, hp 1000, at 0 0 0): they count as enemies, so she
# called for help in the range's anteroom as soon as Leon walked off (tester's report 24.10.2026
# 00:12, Retroid, 0.9.0-beta; the merchant em18 sets the flag, the targets did not). The final
# game keeps her quiet there. Fixed: targets carry EM_STATUS_ASHLEY_NO_HELP too (they are never a
# danger to her). Decision of the project owner 22.10.2026: prototype bugs that the final game
# does not have are fixed.
--- a/src/em3e/em3e.cpp
+++ b/src/em3e/em3e.cpp
@@ -37,6 +37,9 @@
 cEmMark::cEmMark()
 {
     setStatus(EM_STATUS_LOCKOFF);
+    /* PORT (patch 0110, a bug of the prototype): a target or a gate of the shooting range is no
+       enemy for Ashley's call for help (cSubChar's S_EM_NEAR2, pl_npc.cpp). */
+    setStatus(EM_STATUS_ASHLEY_NO_HELP);
 }
 
